 "preregistration": {
  "AMENDMENT": "Amended once, after a one-flight-per-arm pipeline smoke test and BEFORE the campaign was run. Two changes, both recorded here rather than silently applied. (1) The per-flight statistic was originally the whole monitored window; that window contains 40 s of pre-injection nominal flight in every arm, so it estimated a mixture rather than q_gvalid|h. The conditioning window above replaces it and the original is retained as the secondary. (2) The smoke test showed ArduPilot's own EKF failsafe switching to LAND 8.8 s after denial, which eventually disarms the vehicle and truncates the observation window in the fault arms only. Raising FS_EKF_THRESH did not stop it (the readback is recorded per flight), so rather than fight the autopilot the conditioning window is sized to fit inside the armed segment the failsafe leaves, and the mode changes are recorded as an observable in their own right. What the smoke test showed of the outcome: denial closed the gate, glitch did not.",
  "arm_statistic": "mean over flights (flight is the independence unit, NOT the tick: closure is autocorrelated within a flight)",
  "arm_time_s": 20.0,
  "bootstrap_resamples": 10000,
  "bootstrap_seed": 20260823,
  "conditioning_window": "[injection_time_s, injection_time_s + 25 s]. The hypothesis label is the injection state, so the window over which q_gvalid|h is estimated must be the window in which h holds. In the nominal arm the same instant passes with no parameter applied, so the window is [60 s, 85 s] in every arm and the design is matched. 25 s is chosen because ArduPilot's own EKF failsafe switches to LAND under GNSS loss and the vehicle eventually disarms; the window is sized to sit inside the armed segment that leaves, in every arm.",
  "conditioning_window_s": 25.0,
  "flight_end_s": 120.0,
  "gvalid_closed_at_tick": "TrustState.edges['altitude_baro'][1] == 0.0 (online.py:517-518 gates that edge on gvalid alone, so it is a direct readout of the gate)",
  "injection_time_s": 60.0,
  "interval_method": "BCa over flights for each arm; PAIRED percentile for the ratio (the arms share flight specs, so the resample is over spec index)",
  "min_flights_for_inference": 5,
  "min_window_coverage": 0.95,
  "monitored_tick": "armed is True AND layer time >= arm_time_s",
  "n_flights_per_arm": 6,
  "per_flight_statistic": "closed monitored ticks in the conditioning window / monitored ticks in the conditioning window",
  "secondary_statistic": "the same ratio over the whole monitored window, which dilutes the fault arms with their own pre-injection nominal segment and is reported only for completeness",
  "tick_hz": 25.0
 },
